## Summary
Prosecutors in Liguria, Italy, allege that regional governor Giovanni Toti and his cabinet head Matteo Cozzani manipulated COVID-19 infection numbers. Toti reportedly admitted to slightly increasing the case numbers. The manipulation's purpose and extent are under investigation.

## Key Points
- Liguria's governor Giovanni Toti allegedly manipulated COVID-19 case numbers.
- Toti confessed to increasing case numbers in a conversation with Matteo Cozzani.
- Prosecutors are investigating the extent and purpose of the data manipulation.


